    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7019a4e3_4d8dbc7e",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/NetworkTemplate.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 373,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-23T09:22:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this won\u0027t behave as it did historically, at least strictly speaking.\n\nThe old code would actually try and match specifically a null subscriber ID if you called this with null, because the match rule would be EXACT_MATCH.\n\nSo for a line in the data usage that has both a wifi network key and a subscriber ID, it would now match, while it wouldn\u0027t match before.\n\nThis is unlikely to be a concrete issue, but if someone was to call this with null instead of the version above, it\u0027s likely because they actually want to exclude wifis with a subscriber ID (barring, of course, code organization reasons where they\u0027d want to unify the code paths and pass null when they don\u0027t have one in the hopes of getting them all)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 373,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 373,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "8eb37a5ddb9a5eb7831b0bfb6ae3dc97cb056e3c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
